00-sources/*.pdf
00-sources/originals/*.pdf
*.zip
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# 00-sources/md/ and 00-sources/pages/ ARE tracked, by decision 2026-08-14.
# Both are byte-identical across rebuilds, so they diff meaningfully and a
# reader can see a source without building anything.
#
# These two are not, and cannot be:
#
#   source.db     182 MB. GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MiB, so this
#                 cannot be pushed without Git LFS. Rebuild it in ~20 seconds:
#                     python tools/build_source_corpus.py
#   page-images/  a render cache, filled on request at ~1-3 MB per page. It
#                 would grow without limit and holds nothing that is not in
#                 the PDFs already.
00-sources/source.db
00-sources/source.db-wal
00-sources/source.db-shm
00-sources/page-images/

# Derived views of the Thaqalayn snapshots. md/ and pages/ are tracked for the
# PDF corpus because they are the only readable form of a source whose original
# is not in the repository. That reason does not hold here: 00-sources/api/*.jsonl
# IS the source, it is plain text, and it diffs. These two would be 32 MB of
# exact duplication of it — and the API editions have no page boundaries for a
# pages/ file to record in the first place. Rebuilt by build_source_corpus.py.
00-sources/md/SRC-TQ-*.md
00-sources/pages/SRC-TQ-*.pages.jsonl

# Raw upstream OCR for SRC-IRS-003. Untracked for the same reason the PDFs are:
# it is the original, it is re-downloadable from archive.org's "kitab-al-irshad"
# item, and the thing this project actually reads —
# 00-sources/text/irshad--howard-book-of-guidance.txt — is derived from it,
# tracked, and diffable.
00-sources/*-djvu.txt
